From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: don't disable the PCI interrupts twice

disable_irq() nests, and the driver enables its interrupts once per start.
A firmware crash during a restart reaches ath11k_core_reset() with the
interrupts still disabled by the reset before it, as they are only enabled
once the firmware is up. So does ath11k_core_suspend_late() after a restart
that failed. The second disable leaves the interrupts masked after the next
start, the restart then times out connecting to the firmware, and so does
every restart after it, until a reboot.

This is from reading the code. A reset after a WoW suspend, which disabled
the interrupts the same way, was seen to end like that:

  ath11k_pci 0006:01:00.0: failed to receive control response completion, polling..
  ath11k_pci 0006:01:00.0: Service connect timeout
  ath11k_pci 0006:01:00.0: failed to connect to HTT: -110

Skip the disable when the flags say the interrupts are disabled already.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pcic.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pcic.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pcic.c
index 2259adc3b..8a4bf6327 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pcic.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pcic.c
@@ -379,7 +379,9 @@ static void ath11k_pcic_ce_irqs_disable(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 {
 	int i;
 
-	clear_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_CE_IRQ_ENABLED, &ab->dev_flags);
+	/* A disable nests, and a restart may have stopped short of the enable. */
+	if (!test_and_clear_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_CE_IRQ_ENABLED, &ab->dev_flags))
+		return;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ab->hw_params.ce_count; i++) {
 		if (ath11k_ce_get_attr_flags(ab, i) & CE_ATTR_DIS_INTR)
@@ -450,7 +452,9 @@ static void __ath11k_pcic_ext_irq_disable(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 {
 	int i;
 
-	clear_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_EXT_IRQ_ENABLED, &ab->dev_flags);
+	/* Likewise, see ath11k_pcic_ce_irqs_disable(). */
+	if (!test_and_clear_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_EXT_IRQ_ENABLED, &ab->dev_flags))
+		return;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ATH11K_EXT_IRQ_GRP_NUM_MAX; i++) {
 		struct ath11k_ext_irq_grp *irq_grp = &ab->ext_irq_grp[i];
